94 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (Create a Python application to be used inside ArcGIS Pro. Produce a tool that could be used by city planners to identify areas where tree cover could mitigate urban heat island effect with a Planting Priority Index \(PPI\).)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
95 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (Our tool allows the user to select a city and produces a suitability analysis using weighted variables. For our variables, we chose to look at pre-existing canopy cover, impervious surfaces, and land surface temperature. The remote sensing data for these variables was collected using Google Earth Engine.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
96 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (The framework for our program was made with Model Builder in ArcGIS Pro. We exported the model to a Python script to fine-tune the process. Each variable was reclassified to represent the need for trees, for instance, cells with high pre-existing tree canopy cover were given lower priority than cells with fewer trees. The sum of these variables gives us the final PPI. The output is a raster showing areas of high and low priority.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
97 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 73 0 R
/T (Procedure)
/E (Procedure)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
98 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (Planting Priority Index results: Boston \(left\), shows a cluster of high PPI near the city center, while Phoenix \(right\) has a higher need in general, with the highest values along the I-10 corridor.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
