151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 80 0 R
/E (Previous work found a seasonal trend with nitrates, associated with fertilizer use. Our data did not support any seasonal trends. Instead, it appears to be a long-term, consistent source of pollution. Based on the spatial trends, we found that high levels were associated with livestock production, particularly pig farms. We suspect that long-term leakage from faulty waste lagoons could be responsible for much of the nitrate and nitrite pollution. Nutrient pollution like nitrates can cause algal blooms that are a danger to both ecological and human health. Models like ours can be used to target pollution sources and create mitigation strategies.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
